          },
          "authorityIds": "col:QJ5F,wfo:wfo-0000762950",
          "description": "Campynemanthe viridiflora is the type species of the genus Campynemanthe, first described by Henri Baillon in 1893. It is a perennial herb or subshrub 20–30 cm tall with distinctive greenish (viridulous) tepals and curved staminal filaments that give the genus its name. Endemic to New Caledonia, it occurs on serpentine substrates in wet montane forests of the southern part of Grande Terre, including Mount Mou. Like its congeners, it is a relictual monocot representing an early-diverging lineage within the order Liliales.",
          "authorship": "Baill., 1893"
        },
