          },
          "authorityIds": "col:5WY37,wfo:wfo-0000762949",
          "description": "Campynemanthe parva is a perennial herb in the family Campynemataceae, described by Peter Goldblatt in 1986. It grows up to 50 cm tall and is distinguished by its elongated leaves. The species is endemic to southeastern New Caledonia, where it occurs in montane wet tropical forests on ultramafic substrates. Like other Campynemanthe species, it is a rhizomatous herb with linear leaves and small greenish trimerous flowers, and represents a relictual Gondwanan lineage within Liliales.",
          "authorship": "Goldblatt, 1986"
        },
