          },
          "authorityIds": "col:QJ5D,wfo:wfo-0000762948",
          "description": "Campynemanthe neocaledonica is a perennial herb or subshrub in the family Campynemataceae (Liliales), endemic to New Caledonia in the southwestern Pacific. It grows as a small, erect, rhizomatous herb with linear to lanceolate leaves and produces small greenish-yellow trimerous flowers in terminal inflorescences. The species is restricted to ultramafic substrates in wet montane forests of southern Grande Terre, occurring in shaded understory at mid-elevations. It represents part of an ancient Gondwanan lineage, one of the most primitive families within the lily order.",
